// v1.0 saved blocks and items by Minecraft 1.0.0's numeric IDs (see
// docs/blocks-and-items.md) with 4-bit data values. This table names the
// modern block or item each one became; src/world/legacy.rs reads it when a
// v1.0 world is first opened in v1.1, and turns the data bits that hold
// orientation, growth or fluid level into block state properties.
//
// An entry with a data value matches only that value; one without matches
// the rest. For blocks the data value is first cut to the bits that pick the
// variant (log and leaf type use the low 2 bits, slab type the low 3).
#![enable(implicit_some)]
